# Line endings must never depend on the checkout platform. Parts of this
# repository read their own sources byte-for-byte: the tokenizer hashes its
# frozen theme inputs against a recorded baseline, and the patch contracts
# match runtime anchors whose patterns contain a literal \n. A CRLF checkout
# breaks both, and only on the platform that produced it — a Windows CI runner
# is what surfaced it. Normalize to LF in the index and on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept explicit because it is the strictest case: these bytes are the frozen
# input to theme tokenization and are identified by their hash.
scripts/theme-sources/*.css text eol=lf

# Bundled binaries must be copied through untouched. `eol` implies `text`, so
# each one has to unset both or the rule above would corrupt it on checkout.
*.woff2 binary !eol
*.ttf   binary !eol
*.png   binary !eol
